AirSnare — Change Log

=============================================================================
0.10.0 (2026-07-28)
=============================================================================

macOS
  - Set the Wi-Fi channel via CoreWLAN (-setWLANChannel:) instead of the
    removed networksetup/airport CLI tools; fixes capture on macOS 15 (Sequoia)

Security / correctness fixes
  - Beacon SSID parsing could read up to ~255 bytes past the packet from a
    crafted beacon; bound the TLV scan and pass the correct length (OOB read)
  - Killer injection failure no longer hangs the capture loop (which also left
    Ctrl-C unresponsive); the loop is now broken on failure
  - pthread_join() no longer writes a pointer into a 4-byte int (stack OOB write)
  - SUDO_UID/GID are parsed strictly; malformed values no longer silently keep
    full root privileges during the privilege drop

Concurrency
  - Deauth injection uses a dedicated pcap handle so the dispatcher thread and
    the main capture loop never share one pcap_t (falls back to the shared one)
  - is_done and log_level are now atomic, out of shared bit-fields

Options / robustness
  - Numeric arguments reject trailing garbage (e.g. "-c 6abc")
  - Live-only/passive checks track CLI presence of -M/-c/-n/-d/-a/-t, so a
    persistent ~/.airsnarerc no longer blocks -r and "-d 5 -n" no longer
    silently discards -d
  - Minor: free the BPF program on setfilter failure; faster shutdown; NUL-safe
    interface name; snprintf instead of sprintf; clearer -x error message

=============================================================================
0.9.0 (2026-04-07)
=============================================================================

Stability fixes
  - BUG-1: add missing return after SUDO_GID error; prevented atoi(NULL) crash
  - BUG-2: try _nobody before nobody on macOS; getpwnam("nobody") returns NULL
    on macOS causing a segfault
  - BUG-3: rename #define abs(x,y) to ZZ_ABS() to avoid clobbering stdlib abs()
  - BUG-4: add _Static_assert for composite hash key alignment in clients.c
  - BUG-5: guard memcpy against NULL ssid and add SSID length bounds check
  - BUG-6: use arc4random_uniform() on macOS instead of non-thread-safe rand()
  - BUG-7: zz_error() now returns 0 consistently (was accidentally returning 1,
    inverting all error paths that used it)
  - BUG-8: remove redundant is_live guard inside is_live branch in handler.c

macOS functionality
  - MACOS-1: channel setting via networksetup with automatic airport fallback
    for Ventura+ where -setairportchannel was removed from networksetup;
    subprocess output suppressed via posix_spawn file actions
  - MACOS-2: explicit error on pcap_inject failure with actionable note about
    passive mode (-n) and external USB adapters for Apple Silicon
  - MACOS-3: descriptive error and hint when pcap_set_rfmon fails; guides user
    toward -M flag and SIP considerations
  - MACOS-4: replace deprecated setitimer/SIGALRM with kqueue EVFILT_TIMER
    and EVFILT_SIGNAL on macOS

Protocol features
  - PROTO-1: add Reassociation Request/Response frames (0x20, 0x30) to BPF
    filter; reset per-client handshake state on reassociation
  - PROTO-2: parse RSN IE from beacon tagged parameters to detect PMF
    capability bits (MFPC bit 7, MFPR bit 6); warn when targeting APs that
    require management frame protection
  - PROTO-3: expose handshake_timeout as a configuration key (default 500 ms);
    controls the maximum time window between consecutive EAPOL messages
  - PROTO-4: extract PMKID from EAPOL Message 1 key data (KDE wire format
    DD 14 00:0F:AC 04 <16 bytes>); log in hashcat 22000 format (WPA*01*...)
    for offline cracking without a full 4-way handshake

Code quality
  - INT-1: fall back to getpwuid(getuid())->pw_dir when HOME is unset in
    config file ~ expansion; handles sudo configurations that do not
    forward HOME
  - INT-2: move ZZ_LOG_LEVEL_NAMES[] definition from static-in-header to
    terminal.c; log.h now uses extern declaration to avoid per-TU copies
  - INT-3: remove legacy zz_out/zz_log aliases from terminal.h; all callers
    updated to zz_info/zz_debug
  - INT-4: eliminate static pcap_t *pcap global and terminate_pcap_loop()
    async signal handler; SIGINT and SIGTERM are now blocked in the main
    thread and delivered to the dispatcher thread, which calls
    pcap_breakloop(zz->pcap) directly using its zz argument
    (kqueue EVFILT_SIGNAL on macOS, sigwait set on Linux)

